title Caravan arrive -- a phase may arrive after the plan is seated, in one bounded pass
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the increment
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md end to end -- every row carries all three fields and a closure, #80's booked count guard stands as tools/crypto_count_guard_witness.rish, #85's loom stands as tools/witness_claim_check_witness.rish with its two honest ratchets named. No open agent-closable red, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came from the newest log's own recommend rather than from REMEMBER alone -- arrange.rye had just closed, and it named its successor exactly: every rung in this arc reasons over a queue handed whole before the first child starts, so work arriving after the seating has no door at all.
think Council rota by lap index -- 476 .kyri logs on disk, this is lap 477, and 477 mod 27 = 18, so the deep-read was context/TWO_ROOMS.md. Its law shaped what this rung claims out loud: a phase joining a plan whose children are already in flight belongs to the vision room until a witness binds it, so the module names that limit plainly rather than borrowing the bench's confidence for it. What the bench proves here is the door and its cost.
think The reading itself. An arrival is a claim about one phase, so it should cost one walk rather than a seating. Three facts decide it, and each is a fact about the same phases -- whether anyone placed was waiting for this turn, how many of its steps already stand, and what those steps already said about the turns they follow -- so one Standing struct gathers all three in a single pass, max_arrival_tests = max_queue_len against max_seating_tests = max_queue_len squared, asserted strictly less at comptime.
think The scan reads declared masks rather than their closing, and that is enough: a turn reaches the newcomer transitively only through some turn that names it outright, and any such turn either stands in this plan -- where the scan sees its own declaration -- or stands outside it, where it holds nothing. That argument is written into the function's own comment so a later reader need not rediscover it.
think Naming, under the Comlink tendency and the Lexicon's opening line. join was taken by the Lotus audio family (lotus/join.rye and five kin), so arrive was drawn instead -- plain, warm, unclaimed anywhere in the tree, and it says what the phase does rather than what the queue does to it.
obs A plan grown one arrival at a time is the plan its author wrote, phase for phase, and it seats to itself -- so this rung generalizes arrange.rye rather than rivalling it, the same identity an empty turn mask had to the sibling mask and a seated plan had to its own arranging. That test is this arc's standing shape, now one tier further out.
obs The refusal names a real order rather than a shy reading, and the selftest proves both halves: a phase of turn 4 arriving behind turn 5 -- which names it -- is refused, while the same phase arriving ahead of turn 5 is welcome at the tail. A door that refused both would have been conservative rather than correct.
obs The cost is printed from the bounds themselves rather than typed into prose -- 6 arrivals at most 96 tests against 1536 to seat the plan again each time -- so the claim cannot drift from the code the way a spelled-out count did in REDS #80.
obs The limit is named rather than implied. The arrivals here are weighed at the door, before the run begins; carrying one into a supervisor with children already in flight is the next rung's question. TWO_ROOMS is why that sentence is in the module banner, the README, and the witness header alike.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim. Letting the door stop noticing who was waiting reds the pure read in the happy zone with no child started; silencing that read as well fires the run's own assert(plan_is_seated) at caravan/arrive.rye:341, so the invariant is load-bearing rather than decorative. Letting the door stop checking a turn's step order reds at a phase skipping the step its own turn had open.
obs Thirty-six green-witnessed Rye rings now carry the Microkit shape across real processes. TAME surface GREEN -- style bans clean, width-check exit 0 -- and the neighbor rung re-GREEN: caravan_arrange_witness passed unchanged beside the new one.
loom witness=caravan_arrive_witness arrivals=6 arrival_tests_max=96 seating_tests_max=1536 passes=1 slots_unspent=6 reaped=7 out_of_precede=0 children_started_on_refusal=0
file caravan/arrive.rye the rung -- arrival_admits reads a plan once and answers three facts; arrive and grow build a plan a phase at a time; run_with_arrivals answers by name at the door
file tools/caravan_arrive_witness.rish the witness on metal -- native contains checks, both RED paths recorded in the header
file caravan/README.md the durable Arrive section, placed before Held, carrying the numbers and the named limit
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moved to this rung; the arrange edge folded into the prior-edges pointer
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is the one this rung named its own limit -- an arrival is answered at the door, before the run begins, so a supervisor with children already in flight still has no way to take work; the question becomes whether a phase may join a table mid-run without disturbing a slot already granted or a child already started, which wants a lap measuring what an in-flight admission costs against the door's one bounded pass
